  "completed": [
    "The candidate creates exactly six AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET pairs before any future fork: guardian control, reservation ledger, broker report, worker report, guardian release and listener transfer.",
    "All twelve endpoints require root ownership, CLOEXEC, O_RDWR, O_NONBLOCK, connected local seqpacket type and a distinct descriptor and socket identity.",
    "The four final role sets are disjoint and cover every endpoint exactly once: controller 4, broker 3, worker 3 and guardian watch 2. The guardian-prefork set contains the exact eight non-controller endpoints needed before nested child creation.",
    "A clean immediate child must explicitly adopt its inherited topology copy by matching the recorded parent PID in one main-thread process before it may access or transition any endpoint.",
    "Allowed state changes are fixed: initial to controller or guardian-prefork; guardian-prefork to broker, worker or guardian-watch. No alternate role, endpoint injection or second transition is accepted.",
    "Each transition identity-checks all live endpoints, consumes every close once and never retries an ambiguous close. A changed or failed-close socket object is retained so its destructor cannot later close a replacement numeric descriptor.",
    "Snapshots retain only role counts and aggregate state; they contain no descriptor numbers, socket identities, packets, process identifiers or exception text.",
    "Public topology creation remains closed and every process, fork-order, inherited-copy, peer-origin, protocol, reap, native-enforcement, execution and training claim remains false."
  ],
  "fixed_topology": {
    "pairs": 6,
    "endpoints": 12,
    "controller_final_endpoints": 4,
    "guardian_prefork_endpoints": 8,
    "broker_final_endpoints": 3,
